1
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:45,460
[Unsoiled Starlight]

2
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:46,910
[Episode 24]

3
00:00:46,930 --> 00:00:47,460
[Adapted from Migu's novel
“Unsoiled Starlight” ]

4
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:47,960
[Original Writer: Shan Gu Jun]

5
00:00:48,350 --> 00:00:51,240
[Notice]

6
00:00:48,830 --> 00:00:49,560
Hi,

7
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:50,870
excuse me.

8
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:53,040
Could I ask if the security guard colleague
working here

9
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:54,780
during the renovation is around?

10
00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:55,680
Colleague?

11
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:56,640
What colleague?

12
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:58,720
I've always been the only one here.

13
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:00,440
He has slightly dark skin

14
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:02,570
and a mole under his right eyebrow.

15
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:04,879
You must be mistaken.

16
00:01:04,879 --> 00:01:05,720
There was no one like that

17
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:06,920
on our security team.

18
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:09,570
Did you set up
a temporary counter outside?

19
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:10,280
No.

20
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:12,280
This is the only place open to the public.

21
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,010
The rest are internal offices.

22
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:24,120
So,

23
00:01:25,070 --> 00:01:26,600
from the very beginning,

24
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,720
the security guards
at the Intellectual Property Center,

25
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:30,520
the staff,

26
00:01:31,039 --> 00:01:32,039
and the documents

27
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:34,080
were all fake.

28
00:01:35,479 --> 00:01:37,240
Someone set a trap for me,

29
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:39,100
leaving me nowhere to escape.

30
00:01:39,890 --> 00:01:42,690
They were just
waiting for me to walk right into it.

31
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,560
Who hates me this much,

32
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:46,950
and would go to such lengths

33
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:50,160
just to bring about my downfall?

34
00:01:53,930 --> 00:01:54,860
Don't be afraid.

35
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:56,200
I'm here.

36
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:59,960
Even if Lisen holds you accountable
for the two million loss,

37
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:01,320
I will cover it for you.

38
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:03,640
Zhuo Yu'an,

39
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:08,340
are you going to fix things
for me every time from now on?

40
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,760
This is my own mistake,

41
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:15,740
and I want to take responsibility for it.

42
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:19,120
Do you have to draw
such a clear line with me?

43
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:23,170
I just don't want to hide behind others

44
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:26,040
and be a coward.

45
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:48,079
Hi, Mom.

46
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,320
Where are you?

47
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:53,820
I'm dealing with something outside.
What's wrong?

48
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:55,020
Come back quickly.

49
00:02:55,079 --> 00:02:56,050
About your marriage,

50
00:02:56,050 --> 00:02:57,320
we all know.

51
00:03:17,150 --> 00:03:18,800
Long time no see, Tinglan.

52
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,130
Why are you everywhere?

53
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:23,560
I'm here for work.

54
00:03:24,150 --> 00:03:25,079
What about you?

55
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:29,079
Looks like you've had a rough time

56
00:03:29,079 --> 00:03:30,560
while I was away.

57
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:33,579
Those dark circles under your eyes
are pretty bad.

58
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:38,170
Do you have to keep staring at me
like that?

59
00:03:47,370 --> 00:03:48,430
Your hair's a mess.

60
00:03:49,170 --> 00:03:50,160
It's in the way.

61
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,480
Good luck.

62
00:03:56,350 --> 00:03:57,200
Tinglan.

63
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:13,340
The patent author is suing.

64
00:04:13,370 --> 00:04:14,620
You won't win this case,

65
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:15,800
so just pay up.

66
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:18,360
Mr. Gao.

67
00:04:26,790 --> 00:04:27,380
Lawyer Xiao,

68
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:28,440
Take a look.

69
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:37,190
It's impossible to win this.

70
00:04:37,190 --> 00:04:38,880
But this is our last chance.

71
00:04:55,990 --> 00:04:56,880
Lawyer Xiao.

72
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,760
Just let me try.

73
00:05:03,530 --> 00:05:04,160
Tell me,

74
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:05,310
how should you

75
00:05:05,310 --> 00:05:06,240
solve this?

76
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:08,480
Divorce.

77
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:09,640
Come on.

78
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:12,200
Impossible.

79
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:15,240
Do you know who she is?

80
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:17,040
She is my wife.

81
00:05:17,570 --> 00:05:18,520
Besides you two,

82
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:20,800
she is the closest person to me.

83
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:21,460
What a joke.

84
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,040
This woman...

85
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:27,980
can never marry into
the Zhuo family anyway.

86
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:29,240
Why?

87
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:33,800
Because she is Shu Minghai's daughter.

88
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:38,600
Shu-Shu Minghai?

89
00:05:39,159 --> 00:05:41,520
Your former subordinate, Shu Minghai?

90
00:05:41,950 --> 00:05:43,080
Who else could it be?

91
00:05:44,850 --> 00:05:45,520
Mom,

92
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:47,760
what happened before?

93
00:05:49,409 --> 00:05:50,280
Yu'an,

94
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:52,500
I can't help you this time.

95
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:54,760
This person

96
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,520
has been the biggest worry

97
00:05:56,520 --> 00:05:58,650
for your father and me all these years.

98
00:05:58,800 --> 00:05:59,560
He was

99
00:05:59,810 --> 00:06:02,530
just an ordinary employee
in your dad's company at the time.

100
00:06:02,530 --> 00:06:04,240
Relying on
your dad's appreciation and promotion,

101
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:05,840
he made his way up to manager.

102
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:08,030
Mr. Zhuo,

103
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:09,820
thank you for trusting me

104
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:11,640
and giving me such a big project.

105
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:15,640
Minghai.

106
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:18,250
Remember

107
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:19,500
to be rational.

108
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:20,560
Okay.

109
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:22,820
I will definitely keep it in mind.

110
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:24,840
Mr. Zhuo.

111
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:26,280
We understand

112
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:27,670
that you value talented people.

113
00:06:27,670 --> 00:06:29,680
But when you place so much in an outsider,

114
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,200
trusting him in every way,

115
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:32,640
Where dose that

116
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,000
leave us old-timers?

117
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:36,280
Survival of the fittest

118
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,720
is the basic rule of Zhuo Group

119
00:06:39,140 --> 00:06:41,000
and the law of capital operation.

120
00:06:41,230 --> 00:06:43,080
If you feel a sense of crisis,

121
00:06:43,610 --> 00:06:45,680
you should talk less and do more.

122
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:51,960
He got to know all kinds of dignitaries
through your dad.

123
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:52,720
Gradually,

124
00:06:52,830 --> 00:06:54,090
as his wings grew full,

125
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:55,460
he was no longer willing

126
00:06:55,460 --> 00:06:57,060
to be subordinate to others.

127
00:06:57,130 --> 00:06:58,330
It wasn't long before

128
00:06:58,630 --> 00:07:00,160
he started his own company.

129
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:02,300
[EPC Project of Intelligence]
[Open auction]

130
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:09,240
At this public bidding event,

131
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:12,240
congratulations
to Mr. Shu on winning the bid.

132
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:14,740
Congratulations!

133
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Survival of the fittest.

134
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,200
You deserve it.

135
00:07:22,140 --> 00:07:26,420
[EPC Project of Intelligence]
[Open Bidding]

136
00:07:23,760 --> 00:07:26,290
He also took various projects
from the group.

137
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:28,160
But he

138
00:07:29,110 --> 00:07:30,310
only knows how to work

139
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:32,930
but is not good at
operation and management.

140
00:07:32,930 --> 00:07:33,600
Soon,

141
00:07:33,950 --> 00:07:35,360
the company fell apart

142
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:37,440
and was on the verge of bankruptcy.

143
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:38,840
He came to your dad again.

144
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:40,040
Mr. Zhuo,

145
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:43,480
My company is a little short
on cash right now.

146
00:07:44,300 --> 00:07:47,159
We urgently need
a guarantee deposit for a project.

147
00:07:48,159 --> 00:07:49,520
Could you help me out?

148
00:07:56,990 --> 00:07:57,880
Okay.

149
00:08:00,170 --> 00:08:01,200
Thank you.

150
00:08:03,110 --> 00:08:04,720
Your dad was only tring to

151
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:06,360
help him out.

152
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:08,540
But who would've thought

153
00:08:08,580 --> 00:08:11,680
he was really looking to
have your father share the risk?

154
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:12,400
In the end,

155
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:14,500
the company still went bankrupt,

156
00:08:14,610 --> 00:08:16,480
leaving over 100 million yuan in debt.

157
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,720
And then he fled.

158
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:18,880
Zhuo Group

159
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:20,480
had to take on all the debt.

160
00:08:20,870 --> 00:08:22,200
This caused quite a stir

161
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:24,440
among the board members.

162
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:27,390
Your father was
under a lot of pressure.

163
00:08:27,390 --> 00:08:29,440
It took him years to pay off the debt.

164
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:30,920
After that,

165
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:33,309
he never trusted outsiders again.

166
00:08:57,890 --> 00:08:58,690
What's wrong?

167
00:09:00,950 --> 00:09:02,280
I went to see my parents.

168
00:09:04,310 --> 00:09:05,910
Did they give you a hard time?

169
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:08,560
No.

170
00:09:25,170 --> 00:09:26,080
Zhuo Yu'an.

171
00:09:33,310 --> 00:09:34,400
Thank you.

172
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:39,940
Can you change "thank you"

173
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:42,040
to another three words?

174
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,560
I love you.

175
00:09:58,700 --> 00:09:59,640
Shu Tinglan.

176
00:10:00,070 --> 00:10:01,000
Yeah?

177
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:02,920
Between us,

178
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:05,770
we don't need to draw such clear lines.

179
00:10:08,970 --> 00:10:11,430
I want to face many things
together with you.

180
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:23,380
Don't leave me.

181
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:47,760
This is why I asked you to leave her.

182
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:51,040
But Dad,

183
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:54,240
Shu Tinglan is innocent.

184
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:55,600
I don't think so.

185
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:58,400
Shu Minghai was heavily in debt

186
00:10:58,480 --> 00:10:59,840
and had bad conduct.

187
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,960
He kept another woman on the side

188
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:03,560
and even had a child with her.

189
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:05,960
A child growing up in such an environment,

190
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:08,200
no matter how good-natured she may be,

191
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:10,840
will be influenced by it.

192
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:11,610
Dad,

193
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:14,000
You haven't even met her.

194
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:16,040
How can you tell if she's good or bad?

195
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:17,160
Yu'an,

196
00:11:17,890 --> 00:11:20,260
after so many years of hard work,

197
00:11:20,290 --> 00:11:21,560
our group has built

198
00:11:21,830 --> 00:11:24,100
a precise and efficient operating system

199
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:25,720
that is stable and secure.

200
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:28,330
And you will
inherit the group in the future.

201
00:11:28,330 --> 00:11:29,760
If you marry the daughter of a traitor

202
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:31,690
who harmed the group's interests,

203
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:34,850
how can I explain to
the board of directors

204
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:36,600
and the group members?

205
00:11:39,160 --> 00:11:40,120
Alright, don't be mad.

206
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:41,040
Don't be mad.

207
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,060
It's getting cold.

208
00:11:42,060 --> 00:11:43,720
I told you to dress warmer.

209
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:44,320
Let's go.

210
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:46,400
Go back and get some rest.

211
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:50,840
Yu'an.

212
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:53,760
The reason you've grown into
who you are today,

213
00:11:53,950 --> 00:11:56,160
with such
an optimistic and resilient character,

214
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:58,720
is that your mother and I

215
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:01,370
have carefully nurtured you
all these years.

216
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:02,600
I'm old now.

217
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:06,220
I absolutely won't allow
any more accidents to happen.

218
00:12:33,140 --> 00:12:33,800
Mr. Zhuo.

219
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:36,200
Calling this late at night?

220
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:38,000
Your wife won't get jealous?

221
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:39,440
Wen Jian,

222
00:12:40,460 --> 00:12:41,280
let's meet.

223
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:42,480
Sure.

224
00:12:43,110 --> 00:12:44,880
I'd love to see you too.
